title: 'Decided: whether a perspective draws the buffer otherwise is judged by drawing it, at a render per candidate per press.'
pid: 73328c83-107a-4993-b687-bf40fa8ed653
body: |2-
  The first build estimated it from the positions where substitution
  acts, and the review found two ways that went wrong: a switch could
  hide the very nodes that put a later author in the set, so "next"
  skipped that author for good; and an author could join who changed
  nothing, beneath a node shown raw. So each candidate's drawing is
  compared, as text, with the root authors' ('view_text_from'). The
  candidates are the user and the owners of the overriders of what
  either the root authors' drawing or the buffer's own draws, so every
  author found from the default is found from anywhere. Not found: an
  author whose overrides apply only beneath a node another perspective
  puts in place, until that perspective is shown. Unsure: the cost on
  Jeff's large views; nothing measured it.
